# Env Template Rule

Whenever you add or change environment variables, you MUST update the corresponding template file:

| Service | Real env file | Template to update |
|---------|--------------|-------------------|
| CMS (Strapi) | `cms/.env` | `cms/.env.example` |
| Frontend (Next.js) | `frontend/.env.local` | `frontend/.env.local.example` |

## Rules
- Templates use placeholder values only — NEVER put real passwords, keys, or secrets in templates
- Use descriptive placeholders: `your-mailbox-password`, `your-api-key-here`, not `tobemodified`
- Add a comment above each group explaining what the vars are for and where to get them
- Both template files are committed to the repo; both real env files are gitignored
